{
  "slug": "tts-attention-alert",
  "name": "Tts Attention Alert",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Windows-only attention alerts for AI coding agents. When the agent pauses for permission, asks a question, or finishes a response, the plugin speaks the notification out loud (TTS) and pulses a colored frame around your primary monitor — gold for blocking events, escalating to orange and red if you don't respond within 20s and 40s. Stop events get a calmer blue 3-pulse. Auto-ducks Spotify, YouTube, VLC, and other media apps around the spoken phrase so the alert is audible even mid-song, then resumes them. A forensic log of every event is written to ~/.claude/cache/notifications.log so you can scroll back what fired while you were away. No external dependencies — pure System.Speech.Synthesis, WPF, and WinRT GlobalSystemMediaTransportControlsSessionManager.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (3): `mute-tts-status` (Report which tts-attention-alert mute scopes are currently active by reading ~/.claude/settings.json), `mute-tts` (Mute the tts-attention-alert plugin), `unmute-tts` (Unmute the tts-attention-alert plugin)\n- **Hooks** (4): `Notification`, `PreToolUse`, `PermissionRequest`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install tts-attention-alert@claude-community` from `PettHa/tts-attention-alert`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 3
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
